{"evidence":[{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Lucy Muringo Gichuhi (née Munyiri) ( ) (born 23 September 1962) is an Australian politician who is a Senator for South Australia, sitting as an independent.","title":"Lucy Gichuhi"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" She was declared to have been elected at the 2016 election for the Family First Party following a special recount on 13 April 2017 ordered by the High Court of Australia, sitting as the Court of Disputed Returns, following its decision that Bob Day had not been eligible to stand for election.","title":"Lucy Gichuhi"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"The Story of Lucy Gault is a novel written by William Trevor in 2002.","title":"The Story of Lucy Gault"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" The book is divided into three sections: the childhood, middle age and older times of the girl, Lucy.","title":"The Story of Lucy Gault"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" The story takes place in Ireland during the transition to the 21st century.","title":"The Story of Lucy Gault"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" It follows the protagonist Lucy and her immediate contacts.","title":"The Story of Lucy Gault"},{"sentence_id":4,"text":" The book was shortlisted for the Booker and Whitbread Prizes in 2002.","title":"The Story of Lucy Gault"},{"sentence_id":5,"text":" ","title":"The Story of Lucy Gault"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Saint Lucy's Day, also called the Feast of Saint Lucy, is a Christian feast day celebrated on 13 December in Advent, commemorating Saint Lucy, a 3rd-century martyr under the Diocletianic Persecution, who according to legend brought "food and aid to Christians hiding in the catacombs" using a candle-lit wreath to "light her way and leave her hands free to carry as much food as possible".","title":"Saint Lucy's Day"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" Her feast once coincided with the Winter Solstice, the shortest day of the year before calendar reforms, so her feast day has become a Christian festival of light.","title":"Saint Lucy's Day"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" Falling within the Advent season, Saint Lucy's Day is viewed as an event signaling the arrival of Christmastide, pointing to the arrival of the Light of Christ in the calendar, on Christmas Day.","title":"Saint Lucy's Day"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Bob Day (born 1952) is a politician and businessman in South Australia, Australia.","title":"Bob Day (disambiguation)"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Ramblin' Gamblin' Man is the first studio album by American rock band the Bob Seger System, released in 1969 (see 1969 in music).","title":"Ramblin' Gamblin' Man"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" The original title was "Tales of Lucy Blue", hence the cover photo.","title":"Ramblin' Gamblin' Man"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" In the liner notes, Bob Seger says (sarcastically) he later realized Lucy Blue was Ramblin' Gamblin' Man, and so changed the title of the album.","title":"Ramblin' Gamblin' Man"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" He then thanks "Doctor Fine" for this realization.","title":"Ramblin' Gamblin' Man"},{"sentence_id":4,"text":" (Doctor Fine being the person who made Seger change the album's name.)","title":"Ramblin' Gamblin' Man"},{"sentence_id":5,"text":" The original cover design for the album featured the nude figure from Botticelli's "The Birth of Venus", but this too was changed for the final release.","title":"Ramblin' Gamblin' Man"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":""Bob Day Afternoon" is the second episode of the second season of the animated comedy series "Bob's Burgers" and the overall 15th episode, and is written by Dan Fybel and Rich Rinaldi and directed by Wes Archer.","title":"Bob Day Afternoon"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" It aired on Fox in the United States on March 18, 2012.","title":"Bob Day Afternoon"}],"peer_messages":["Unverified peer answer: Bob Day
