{"evidence":[{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Linda Stender (born July 25, 1951) is an American Democratic Party politician who has served in the New Jersey General Assembly from 2002 to 2016, where she represented the 22nd legislative district.","title":"Linda Stender"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" She ran unsuccessfully for a seat in the United States House of Representatives, seeking to represent New Jersey's 7th District, in 2006 and 2008.","title":"Linda Stender"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" She was narrowly defeated by incumbent Representative Mike Ferguson in 2006 but lost by a wider margin to Leonard Lance in the November 4, 2008 election.","title":"Linda Stender"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"The New Jersey Folk Festival is an annual folk music and cultural festival held on the Great Lawn of the Eagleton Institute of Politics on the Douglass Campus at Rutgers University in New Brunswick, New Jersey.","title":"New Jersey Folk Festival"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" It is a free, non-profit family event held every year on the last Saturday in April from 10am - 6pm, rain or shine.","title":"New Jersey Folk Festival"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" It coincides with Rutgers Agricultural Field Day held on the adjacent Cook Campus.","title":"New Jersey Folk Festival"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" Beginning in 2009, both the New Jersey Folk Festival and Ag Field Day are held as a major part of Rutgers Day.","title":"New Jersey Folk Festival"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Leonard Cooke (born April 29, 1982) is an American former high school and professional basketball player.","title":"Lenny Cooke"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" Born in Atlantic City, New Jersey, he is known primarily for having been ranked higher than LeBron James and Carmelo Anthony in the Summer of 2001.","title":"Lenny Cooke"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" He had averaged 25 points, 10 rebounds, two steals, and two blocks per game in his junior year of high school.","title":"Lenny Cooke"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" Following his junior year in high school, he averaged 31.5 points for the first eight games of his senior year.","title":"Lenny Cooke"},{"sentence_id":4,"text":" When he turned 19 in 2001, he was academically ineligible to play according to high school athletics' rules in his home county in New Jersey.","title":"Lenny Cooke"},{"sentence_id":5,"text":" Cooke is the subject of the 2013 Tribeca Film Festival selected documentary film "Lenny Cooke" by the Safdie Brothers.","title":"Lenny Cooke"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Leonard J. Lance (born June 25, 1952) is the U.S. Representative for New Jersey 's 7 congressional district , serving since 2009.","title":"Leonard Lance"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" He is a member of the Republican Party.","title":"Leonard Lance"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" He previously served in the New Jersey Senate and the New Jersey General Assembly where he had been lauded by legislative peers as a moderate Republican.","title":"Leonard Lance"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" Since 2009, however, his positions have shifted to conservative Republican positions, such as against environmental regulation, and against Planned Parenthood.","title":"Leonard Lance"},{"sentence_id":4,"text":" He has been a staunch opponent of the Affordable Care Act and against abortion rights; in 2017 he voted against federally funded insurance plans which provide coverage for abortion.","title":"Leonard Lance"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"John Clifford Heed (1862–1908) was an American composer and musician, best known for composing over 60 marches.","title":"John Clifford Heed"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" Born in Hackettstown, New Jersey, on April 23, 1862, Heed began his musical career with the Hackettstown Cornet Band by the age of 11.","title":"John Clifford Heed"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" By the time he reached the age of 17 he was the leader of this band and he had master with astonishing rapidity the intricacies of harmony and counterpoint.","title":"John Clifford Heed"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" He became proficient on the piano and violin, and could play most band instruments.","title":"John Clifford Heed"},{"sentence_id":4,"text":" In 1882 he had the opportunity to travel with a noted English orchestra through the United States.","title":"John Clifford Heed"},{"sentence_id":5,"text":" The cornetist that had come with the orchestra became ill and was sent back to England.","title":"John Clifford Heed"},{"sentence_id":6,"text":" Heed was highly recommended and was engaged to fill his the cornetist's place.","title":"John Clifford Heed"},{"sentence_id":7,"text":" He received encomiums from the press and public in every city and town visited.","title":"John Clifford Heed"},{"sentence_id":8,"text":" A year later, in 1883, Heed accepted an engagement to become the leader of the Providence Brigade Band.","title":"John Clifford Heed"},{"sentence_id":9,"text":" This was a position that he held until he was called back to New Jersey to conduct another orchestra and band.","title":"John Clifford Heed"},{"sentence_id":10,"text":" Soon thereafter, he went to Worcester, Massachusetts and spent eight years as a teacher of bands.","title":"John Clifford Heed"},{"sentence_id":11,"text":" His next position was a cornetist for Voss's First Regiment Band in Newark, New Jersey.","title":"John Clifford Heed"},{"sentence_id":12,"text":" It was after the Metronome article was written that Mr. Heed went with John Phillip Sousa's band as a soloist and arranger before contracting tuberculosis in the 1890s and dying in Newark, New Jersey on February 12, 1908.","title":"John Clifford Heed"},{"sentence_id":13,"text":" He died leaving no children.","title":"John Clifford Heed"},{"sentence_id":14,"text":" He was buried near his family in Union Cemetery in Hackettstown, New Jersey.","title":"John Clifford Heed"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Peter Jacob (born in Kerala, India 1985) was a 2016 Democratic Party candidate in New Jersey's 7th congressional district who ran against Leonard Lance.","title":"Peter Jacob"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" Jacob, a resident of Union, worked as a Licensed Social Worker until he began campaigning full-time.","title":"Peter Jacob"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" Jacob lost the election with 43% of the vote, while Lance was re-elected with 55%.","title":"Peter Jacob"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" The 7th district had been gerrymandered in 2011 to benefit the GOP, with portions of Morris County added, according to a report in NJ.com.","title":"Peter Jacob"}],"peer_messages":["Unverified peer answer: 1951
